igod was given their own two  fingers by the greater will we can see  each of their fingers at their  corresponding Divine Towers all of which  except for Ronnies EG tells us that the  fate of the carrion royal family is  Guided by the stars as is the fate of  Lady Ronnie first Heir in the carrion  Royal line but General radon is the  Conqueror of the stars who stood up to  the swirling constellations halting  their movement in a smashing Victory and  so if General radon were defeated the  Stars would once again resume their  movement as would lady Ronnie's Destiny  so what does it mean when EG says that  Ronnie's fate is Guided by the stars for  a while I sort of thought this just  meant radon held time in place the Stars  wouldn't move meaning that the planet  wouldn't move either but obviously this  doesn't make much sense because there's  a clear night and day cycle and we can  also change the time of day whenever we  wish so that theory is out the window  unless the time of day and the movement  of the stars and the rotation of the  planet are just different in the lands  between that's definitely a long shot  Theory but what makes more sense is that  radon isn't holding back just the stars  but also Ronnie's two fingers in order  for Ronnie to completely rid herself of  all imperian influence she would need to  kill her own two fingers she's already  discarded her body in the ritual during  the night of black knives where her body  and Godwin's Soul were killed her spirit  is free and inherits the doll that  resembles her former Mentor Rena once we  defeat radon the Stars start their  movement once again and we can see a  huge explosion when a shooting star  falls out of the sky which opens up the  secret entrance to nocron the Eternal  City we need to go there in order to  obtain the Finger Slayer blade and give  it to Ronnie the item description of the  blade says the hidden treasure of the  Eternal City of nocron a blade said to  have been born of a corpse 